; bfsodium POLY1305 : the one time authenticator  RFC 8439 section 2 point 5
;
; HAND WRITTEN; acc starts at nought and each sixteen byte block of the message
; with a ONE appended after its bytes is added in and multiplied by the clamped
; r; the tag is the low sixteen bytes of acc plus s;
;
; INTERFACE entry=34 exit=0 footprint=0:413
; IO  in:  key{32}  len{2} LE  msg{len}
;     out: tag{16}
;
; The key is r{16} then s{16}; r is clamped as the RFC requires: bytes 3 7 11
; and 15 keep only their low four bits  and bytes 4 8 and 12 lose their low two;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x11e  the work frame; mulmod136 runs HERE at this file's own zero
;                 and its footprint is 0:286  which is what sets the size of it
;   @0x12c:0x13c  r{17}    the clamped r  copied into the work frame each block
;   @0x140:0x150  s{17}    added in once at the very end
;   @0x154:0x164  acc{17}  the accumulator
;   @0x168:0x178  blk{17}  this block  with the ONE already appended
;   @0x17c:0x17d  rem{2} u16 LE  message bytes not yet taken
;   @0x17e        nz       set while rem is not zero
;   @0x17f        pl       set while this block's ONE still needs placing
;   @0x180        e        the else arm of a choice
;   @0x181        t        a copy  so a count can be tested without being eaten
;   @0x182        u        puts that copy back
;   @0x184        k        sixteen rounds  one per byte position
;   @0x186:0x196  tmp{17}  hands r back after it has been copied
;   @0x19a:0x19d  the clamping halve frame
;
; A byte always lands on the TOP of the block  at blk{16}  and the block then
; slides down one; So a byte taken in round k is shifted sixteen minus k more
; times and comes to rest at blk{k}  which is where it belongs  and the write
; needs no index; Sixteen rounds happen whether or not there are bytes left  so
; the positions come out right for a short block too;
;
; The ONE that ends a block is placed by a flag rather than by an index; pl
; starts at one each block  and the FIRST round that finds no message byte left
; spends it on the top of the block  where it rides down to exactly the place
; the message stopped; A block that fills completely spends it afterwards  just
; past its sixteenth byte;

